    },
    "body": "With substitutes disabled, `guix-codesign` can fail when building [oscrypto](https://pypi.org/project/oscrypto/) 1.3.0. The `test_dump_private` test raises `ZeroDivisionError`.\n\nThe Guix time-machine bump in bitcoin/bitcoin#36233 (merged after the 32.x branch-off) pulls in OpenSSL 3.5.5, which can finish oscrypto's initial PBKDF2 benchmark in under a millisecond. oscrypto truncates this duration to zero and then divides by it. This was fixed upstream in wbond/oscrypto@144c12195001b08b9ccecb8a3fd041d22ae24474\n\nThis PR adds the fix to `contrib/guix/patches`. It can be dropped once a new oscrypto release includes the fix and a Guix time machine bump includes it.",
